 ;; ── Agents: §10 promises them; cljs lacks them because JS has one thread ───────────────────────

 ;; ── Printing and REPL dynamic vars cljs keeps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

 ;; ── Host interop: cljs repointed the word at Closure, we repoint it at the core and its bridges ──

 ;; ── Numbers: cljs dropped the tower, we have it (design §3) ───────────────────────────────────

 ;; ── Arrays: cljs keeps the casts, our array type is the §4 low-level layer ─────────────────────

 ;; ── Chunked seqs: cljs keeps the whole surface ────────────────────────────────────────────────

 ;; ── Hashing: cljs keeps all four, and a user collection must hash like ours ────────────────────

 ;; ── Plain, portable core cljs kept and we simply lack ─────────────────────────────────────────

